{"book":27,"chapter":5,"context":{"chapter":5,"title":"Writing on the Wall","summary":"During a drunken feast using the temple's sacred vessels, King Belshazzar sees a hand write on the wall; Daniel reads the message of judgment, and that night Babylon falls.","background":"Babylonian records show Belshazzar ruled Babylon as co-regent for his father Nabonidus, who spent years away in Arabia. That explains why Daniel is offered the 'third' place in the kingdom (v. 16). Calling Nebuchadnezzar his 'father' (v. 2) fits the ancient use of the word for a royal predecessor. Babylon fell to the Persians under Cyrus in 539 BC.","customs":[{"term":"Mene, tekel, peres","verses":"5:25-28","note":"The words name weights (a mina, a shekel, a half-mina) and also sound like 'numbered,' 'weighed' and 'divided.' Peres also echoes 'Persia.'"}],"watchFor":["The queen (likely the queen mother) remembers Daniel (vv. 10–12).","'Thou... hast not humbled thine heart, though thou knewest all this' (v. 22).","'In that night' (v. 30)."],"connections":["Isaiah 21:9","Jeremiah 51:39","Isaiah 13:17-19"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["בֵּלְשַׁאצַּר","beleshatzar","H1113","ANpm","Belshazzar"],["מַלְכָּא","malka'","H4430","ANcbsd/Ta","king the"],["עֲבַד","'avad","H5648","AVqp3ms","he made"],["לְחֶם","lechem","H3900","ANcbsa","a feast"],["רַב","rav","H7229","AAabsa","great"],["לְרַבְרְבָנוֹהִי","leravrevanohi","H7261","AR/Ncmpc/Sp3ms","for nobles his"],["אֲלַף","'alaf","H506","AAcbsa","a thousand"],["וְלָקֳבֵל","velokovel","H6903","AC/R/Ncbsc","and <to> before"],["אַלְפָּא","'alpa'","H506","AAcbsd/Ta","thousand the"],["חַמְרָא","chamra'","H2562","ANcbsd/Ta","<the> wine"],["שָׁתֵה","shateh","H8355","AVqrmsa","[he was] drinking"]],"x":[[17001003,17001003,6],[1040020,1040020,3],[41006021,41006022,3]],"xn":3},"2":{"w":[["בֵּלְשַׁאצַּר","beleshatzar","H1113","ANpm","Belshazzar"],["אֲמַר","'amar","H560","AVqp3ms","he said"],["בִּטְעֵם","bit'em","H2942","AR/Ncbsc","in [the] taste of"],["חַמְרָא","chamra'","H2562","